# AgentOTelStack application environment example
#
# The infrastructure does not read this file as a Compose secret file. These
# variables are for an application that emits telemetry. Prefer the supported
# launcher (`obs run --service NAME -- COMMAND`), which loads the ingest
# credential and adds the workspace project identity without placing a token in
# the child command line. See docs/CONNECT.md for language-specific setup.

# Host applications (npm run dev, python app.py, and similar):
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4318
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf
OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=my-app
# Manual setup must use the Gateway ingest bearer header. Never use the query
# token here and never connect an app directly to the Collector or a Victoria
# backend.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Bearer%20${GATEWAY_INGEST_TOKEN}

# Manual resource scope. Obtain the canonical workspace UUID with:
#   PROJECT_ID="$(obs project ensure)"
# Then export the complete attribute value in the application environment:
#   OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES="agentotel.project.id=${PROJECT_ID},deployment.environment=dev"
OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=agentotel.project.id=<workspace-project-uuid>,deployment.environment=dev

# Apps inside the Compose edge network use the Gateway service name instead:
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://gateway:4318
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Bearer%20${GATEWAY_INGEST_TOKEN}
# Keep the same OTEL_SERVICE_NAME and agentotel.project.id resource attribute.

# Optional: faster metrics for local development (the bundled demo uses 10s;
# OpenTelemetry SDK defaults may be longer).
# OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL=10000
